      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Cograng",
      "description": "Appearing to the right in the picture of the MV Cill Airne floating restaurant on the river Liffey is the onetime Headquarters of the Black and Tans, officially the Royal Irish Constabulary Special Reserve. The building was attacked in the Irish War of Independence by the IRA in April 1921. \nOfficially called the London and North Western Hotel, it was popularly known as the North Wall Quay hotel. The steamer service to and fro Holyhead in Wales departed from the North Wall Quay. \n\nIn the photograph located behind the floating restaurant is the (closed) North Wall railway station or officially the London and North Western Railway station.",
